            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Anders, aSTRA USA, Inc. (the petitioner) argues that the agreement with Santa Clara County is not an ordinary contract because it functions like a regulatory contract, similar to Medicare provider agreements, where parties agree to abide by statutes and regulations rather than create traditional contract rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Anders",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c648e57d9552f4318752f0dc00920f6c80e1c5d2456c70d62830740e56a66a26",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c648e57d9552-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Anders, the petitioner further contends that permitting third\u2011party\u2011beneficiary suits under such an agreement would interfere with the government\u2019s ability to administer the statutory scheme."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c648e57d9552f4318752f0dc00920f6c80e1c5d2456c70d62830740e56a66a26",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c648e57d9552-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Frederick, santa Clara County (the respondent) argues that Congress intended the agreement to incorporate the full set of common\u2011law contract rights, including third\u2011party\u2011beneficiary rights that have existed for centuries."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c648e57d9552f4318752f0dc00920f6c80e1c5d2456c70d62830740e56a66a26",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c648e57d9552-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Frederick, the respondent emphasizes that departing from normal contract principles would be contrary to precedent such as Winstar, Mobil Oil, Jackson Transit, and Central Airlines."
      }
    ],
